  "result": "Perfect! I've added the VAT summary report:\n\n**src/reports.js** \u2014 Added:\n- **vatSummary(invoices)** \u2014 Returns VAT analysis by rate:\n  - Filters invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n  - For each line in each invoice:\n    - base = line total after discount (clamped at 0)\n    - vat = VAT calculated on the base amount\n  - Groups by VAT rate, accumulating bases and VAT amounts\n  - Returns array of `{ rate, base, vat }`\n  - Sorted by rate descending (highest first)\n\n**Key design:**\n- Base is the taxable amount (after line-level discounts)\n- VAT uses the lineVAT calculation (rounded per line, then summed)\n- Separate tracking by rate for tax reporting\n- All amounts in cents (integer)\n- Excludes draft invoices\n- Includes all issued/paid/partially_paid invoices\n\nAdded 12 tests covering:\n- Single and multiple VAT rates\n- Sorting by rate (highest first)\n- Accumulation across invoices\n- Base calculation with discounts\n- Status filtering\n- Zero VAT (exempt items)\n- Empty results\n- Mixed rates validation\n\nAll 217 tests pass. The invoicing system now has complete reporting: overdue tracking, customer statements, credit notes, and VAT analysis by rate!",
